"""User interface and USB-C: buttons, DIP switch, buzzer, LEDs and the USB-C receptacle.

Buttons (GT-TC048B tactile switches, MCU internal pull-ups), as on the main board:
- SW2 on Button (PA7) with C20 100 nF to GND.
- SW3 on NRST with C21 100 nF to GND, the recommended NRST protection (DS13311 Figure 27
  p168: 0.1 uF; the pin has an internal 30-50 kOhm pull-up, Table 61 p167). The ESP32 also
  drives NRST, open drain (ESP sheet).
BOOT0: R42 10 kOhm (AN5419 Figure 19 p30) and C60 100 nF to GND hold it low, so the MCU always
boots from flash; there is no BOOT0 button.
SW1, a 4-way DIP switch, pulls Switch_0..3 to GND (Switch_0 on PH0, Switch_1-3 on PH1, PC15, PC14,
all with the MCU's internal pull-ups).

Buzzer: BZ1 (FUET-5030, 3 V electromagnetic, externally driven) from 3V3_D through R3 10 Ohm to
the low-side switch Q1 (AO3400A), driven from Buzzer (PA2, TIM15) through R1 220 Ohm with R2
10 kOhm gate pull-down; D3 (1N4148WS, the board's clamp diode, D9-D12) clamps the coil: at most
the 174 mA coil current below, decaying, against its 300 mA IFM and 2 A IFSM at 1 us. R3 is a 1206 (250 mW): at the firmware's
50 % duty and low tones the coil current approaches 3.3 V / (9 + 10) Ohm = 174 mA with the 9 Ohm
minimum coil (FUET-5030 p2), 151 mW in R3.

LEDs:
- D1, D2: WS2812C-2020-V6 addressable LEDs in a chain on 3V3_D (research IR emitters and status
  LEDs; A.4), replacing the main board's WS2815C-2020, whose 9.5-13.5 V supply range fits
  neither 4S nor 3.3 V. DI of D1 on LED_ARGB (PB9, TIM17_CH1), D1 DO to D2 DI. VDD 3.3-5.3 V and
  DI VIH 0.55 x VDD, 1.81-1.84 V on this rail, VIL 0.7 V (Worldsemi WS2812C-2020-V6 datasheet
  V1.1 p3), so PB9 (VOH >= VDD - 0.4 V, VOL <= 0.4 V, DS13311 Table 56) drives it directly with
  1 V and 0.3 V of margin; C19 (D1) and C18 (D2) 100 nF on VDD (p5 typical application). The bit
  timing caps T0L and T1L at 1 us and asks 1.25 us a bit (V1.1 p4), against the WS2815C's 5 us
  (boards/main2/firmware_changes.toml, leds).
  3.3 V operation: the datasheet's tables are at VDD = 5 V; its supply range is 3.3-5.3 V (p3) and
  its features "3.3 V power supply is supported" (p1). Each channel's constant-current sink holds
  4.95-4.99 mA from 0.4 V across it, 4.07 mA at 0.3 V (the Chinese V1.1 p5 "VF" curve, read from
  the figure), so a channel keeps its full 5 mA while its LED's VF is at most VDD - 0.4 V, 2.884 V
  at the rail's 3.284 V minimum. Worldsemi gives no per-colour VF; a comparable InGaN RGB part reads
  2.76 V blue and 2.88 V green at 5 mA (Everlight EAST1616RGBA4 Rev 1, Figures p7-8, typical), so
  red and blue keep full current and green sits at the knee: 4.95 mA for a typical die, about 4.1 mA
  (-18 %) for one 0.1 V higher. At worst white and yellow lean slightly away from green; the colours
  stay recognisable, and the IC starts (rated from 3.3 V, the rail 16 mV below; send the first frame
  1 ms or more after power-up). No addressable LED of this size rates its supply below 3.3 V in its
  electrical table (SK6805-EC20 3.5-5.5 V, XL-2020RGBC-2812B 3.5-5.5 V, SK6812-EC20 3.7-5.5 V,
  WS2816A/C-1313 3.3-5.5 V), and the 12 mA WS2812B-2020-V6 needs more headroom, so the WS2812C
  stays.
- D5 (red) from 3V3_D through R5 680 Ohm, the power indicator: (3.3 V - VF) / 680 Ohm is
  1.3-2.2 mA for the KT-0603R's VF 1.8-2.4 V (LCSC C2286 listing, at its rated current; VF is
  lower at 2 mA), an indicator's brightness at a tenth of its 20 mA rating.
- D4 (blue, KENTO KT-0603B datasheet, LCSC C2288, p3 sections 4-5: VF 2.6-3.1 V and IV
  70-175 mcd at IF = 5 mA, IF 30 mA DC max) from LED_Red (PB12, the firmware's label) through
  R4 100 Ohm. VF rises with IF, so 3.1 V bounds it at every current below 5 mA. PB12's high level
  is VDD - 0.4 V at 8 mA (DS13311 Table 56): at most 0.4 V / 8 mA = 50 Ohm of driver, whose drop
  shrinks with the current. Dimmest (3V3_D 3.284 V, VF 3.1 V, R4 +1 %, 50 Ohm driver):
  (3.284 - 3.1) / (101 + 50) = 1.2 mA, at least 17 mcd at the 70 mcd/5 mA bin's slope (light
  about proportional to IF at low current), against the red D5's 20-33 mcd (300 mcd at 20 mA,
  C2286 listing); brightest (3.346 V, no driver drop, VF 2.6 V, which holds from 5 mA up, R4
  -1 %): 0.746 V / 99 Ohm = 7.5 mA, within the 8 mA of PB12's VOH specification and a quarter of
  the LED's rating; a mid-bin 2.85 V part draws about 4 mA. R4 680 Ohm would leave a 3.1 V die at
  0.25 mA. The datasheet draws no IF-VF curve; a comparable InGaN 0603 blue rises about 0.3 V from
  0 to 10 mA (Everlight 19-217/BHC-ZL1M2RY/6T DSE-0014124 Rev 5 p5, Forward Current vs. Forward
  Voltage, typical), so the dimmest case runs above 1.2 mA in practice. Both LEDs take little of
  the 500 mA USB budget.

USB-C, U2 (GT-USB-7010ASV), a USB 2.0 device port of the ESP32 only (research ESP32 and USB):
- VBUS on +5V: into the power path Q8 (regulators sheet), the ESP32's sense divider (ESP sheet),
  and D8 to GND at the receptacle: SP1005-01ETG (Littelfuse SP1005 Series datasheet, revised
  07/17/19, Electrical Characteristics: VRWM 6.0 V, leakage 0.5 uA max at 5 V, VBR 8.5 V typ at
  1 mA, VC 9.3 V at 1 A and 15.6 V at 10 A, 8/20 us; IPP 8 A; IEC 61000-4-2 +-30 kV contact;
  bidirectional, SOD882, the KiCad SOD-882 land of 0.4 x 0.7 mm pads at 0.7 mm centres holds its
  0.25 x 0.5 mm terminals at 0.65 mm pitch, against the datasheet's 0.325 x 0.65 mm pads at
  0.65 mm). Its stand-off is above the 5.5 V a Type-C source may hold on VBUS (vSafe5V; the +5V
  net's range), so it stays off at any legal VBUS. R6/R7 5.1 kOhm Rd on
  CC1/CC2 (sink). The ESP32 tells the H7 over UART4 when it runs from USB alone.
- D+/D- (USBD_P/USBD_N) from the receptacle through U6 (USBLC6-2SC6, each line in on one I/O pad
  and out on its twin, pins 1/6 and 3/4, so the clamp sits in line) to the ESP32's GPIO20/GPIO19, whose USB PHY needs no
  external termination (ESP sheet). U6's rail pin on 3V3_D, the supply of the circuit it protects
  (USBLC6-2 section 2.2), with C79 100 nF at the part (DocID 11265 Figure 18).
- SBU1/SBU2 open, as Type-C R2.0 section 4.3 (p139) and Table 4-28 (p236) allow: the main board's
  SBU supply for the HM-19 module (Q7, F1, D13, C77, C78, R50-R55, U7) is gone with the module.
- The shell (pads 1-4) on GND.
"""

load("@stdlib/interfaces.zen", "Usb2")
load(
    "./passives.zen",
    "C_100N_0402",
    "LED_BLUE_0603",
    "LED_RED_0603",
    "R_100_0402",
    "R_10K_0402",
    "R_10_1206",
    "R_220_0402",
    "R_5K1_0402",
    "R_680_0402",
)

Capacitor = Module("@stdlib/generics/Capacitor.zen")
Led = Module("@stdlib/generics/Led.zen")
Resistor = Module("@stdlib/generics/Resistor.zen")
Tvs = Module("@stdlib/generics/Tvs.zen")
AO3400A = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/aos/AO3400A/AO3400A.zen")
D1N4148WS = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/cj/1N4148WS/1N4148WS.zen")
DSHP04TJGER = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/kangshen/DSHP04TJGER/DSHP04TJGER.zen")
FUET_5030 = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/fuet/FUET-5030/FUET-5030.zen")
GT_TC048B = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/g-switch/GT-TC048B-H025-L1/GT-TC048B-H025-L1.zen")
GT_USB_7010ASV = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/g-switch/GT-USB-7010ASV/GT-USB-7010ASV.zen")
USBLC6_2SC6 = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/st/USBLC6-2SC6/USBLC6-2SC6.zen")
WS2812C = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/worldsemi/WS2812C-2020/WS2812C-2020.zen")

# Its own sheet in the board schematic (layout/main2.kicad_sch).
Project(name="Peripherals", path="layout", layout=False)

# A signal port takes the name of the board net it carries (the firmware's pin label) wherever
# that name is an identifier, so its sheet pin and hierarchical label match the root's label:
# KiCad's ERC flags labels whose names differ only in case (similar_labels).
V3V3_D = io(Power)
V5V = io(Power)
GND = io(Ground)

Button = io(Net)
Reset = io(Net)
Boot = io(Net)
Switch_0 = io(Net)
Switch_1 = io(Net)
Switch_2 = io(Net)
Switch_3 = io(Net)
Buzzer = io(Net)
LED_ARGB = io(Net)
LED_Red = io(Net)
USB = io(Usb2)

BUZZER_GATE = Net("BUZZER_GATE")
BUZZER_DRAIN = Net("BUZZER_DRAIN")
BUZZER_COIL = Net("BUZZER_COIL")
LED_CHAIN = Net("LED_CHAIN")
LED_BLUE_A = Net("LED_BLUE_A")
LED_RED_A = Net("LED_RED_A")
CC1 = Net("USB_CC1")
CC2 = Net("USB_CC2")

# Buttons and switches.
GT_TC048B(name="SW2", A=GND, B=Button)
Capacitor(name="C20", P1=GND, P2=Button, **C_100N_0402)
GT_TC048B(name="SW3", A=GND, B=Reset)
Capacitor(name="C21", P1=GND, P2=Reset, **C_100N_0402)
Resistor(name="R42", P1=GND, P2=Boot, **R_10K_0402)
Capacitor(name="C60", P1=Boot, P2=GND, **C_100N_0402)
DSHP04TJGER(
    name="SW1",
    S1_A=Switch_0,
    S2_A=Switch_1,
    S3_A=Switch_2,
    S4_A=Switch_3,
    S1_B=GND,
    S2_B=GND,
    S3_B=GND,
    S4_B=GND,
)

# Buzzer.
FUET_5030(name="BZ1", POS=V3V3_D, NEG=BUZZER_COIL)
Resistor(name="R3", P1=BUZZER_DRAIN, P2=BUZZER_COIL, **R_10_1206)
AO3400A(name="Q1", G=BUZZER_GATE, S=GND, D=BUZZER_DRAIN)
Resistor(name="R1", P1=BUZZER_GATE, P2=Buzzer, **R_220_0402)
Resistor(name="R2", P1=GND, P2=BUZZER_GATE, **R_10K_0402)
D1N4148WS(name="D3", A=BUZZER_COIL, K=V3V3_D)

# LEDs. Accepted build warning: 3V3_D's range (3.284-3.346 V, DS13554 Table 6) dips 16 mV below
# the WS2812C's 3.3 V minimum (V1.1 p3); the owner's choice of LED, its 3.3 V operation above.
# Only the LEDs see the rail as 3.3-3.346 V, so the build warns for any other part below its range.
LED_VDD = Power(V3V3_D, voltage="3.3V to 3.346V")
WS2812C(name="D1", VDD=LED_VDD, GND=GND, DI=LED_ARGB, DO=LED_CHAIN)
WS2812C(name="D2", VDD=LED_VDD, GND=GND, DI=LED_CHAIN, DO=NotConnected())
Capacitor(name="C19", P1=GND, P2=V3V3_D, **C_100N_0402)
Capacitor(name="C18", P1=GND, P2=V3V3_D, **C_100N_0402)
Resistor(name="R4", P1=LED_BLUE_A, P2=LED_Red, **R_100_0402)
Led(name="D4", A=LED_BLUE_A, K=GND, **LED_BLUE_0603)
Resistor(name="R5", P1=LED_RED_A, P2=V3V3_D, **R_680_0402)
Led(name="D5", A=LED_RED_A, K=GND, **LED_RED_0603)

# USB-C.
GT_USB_7010ASV(
    name="U2",
    VBUS=V5V,
    GND=GND,
    SHIELD=GND,
    CC1=CC1,
    CC2=CC2,
    SBU1=NotConnected(),
    SBU2=NotConnected(),
    USB=USB,
)
Tvs(
    name="D8",
    package="SOD-882",
    direction="Bidirectional",
    reverse_standoff_voltage="6V",
    mpn="SP1005-01ETG",
    manufacturer="Littelfuse",
    A=GND,
    K=V5V,
)
Resistor(name="R6", P1=GND, P2=CC1, **R_5K1_0402)
Resistor(name="R7", P1=GND, P2=CC2, **R_5K1_0402)
USBLC6_2SC6(name="U6", IO1=USB.D.P, IO2=USB.D.N, VBUS=V3V3_D, GND=GND)
Capacitor(name="C79", P1=GND, P2=V3V3_D, **C_100N_0402)
